    {
      "id": "HI-C68-country",
      "sequence": 2610,
      "title": "देश (desh) — a country",
      "headword": "देश",
      "romanization": "desh",
      "gloss": "a country",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:b41697e08a0f2018",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two words back, from the last run of five: what does ghās mean, and what is कुआँ? You have since filled in a नाम line without a model, and a form asks for more than a name. The next five words are what it asks for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: देश",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "देश (desh) — \"a country\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit देश (desh) (deśa) meant a place, a region, a stretch of land — and it comes from the root दिश् (diś-), \"to point out, to show\". A देश (desh) began as whatever a pointing hand took in."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That root travelled. Latin dīcere, \"to say\", and index, the pointing finger, grew from the same ancient root as दिश्. The finger you use to show someone where you are from is the finger the word is named after."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Every Hindi form you will ever fill in has a देश (desh) line on it, and every conversation that starts with a greeting reaches it within a minute."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five words for saying where you are from."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "say ghās, then read कुआँ and say what it means",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: say *ghās*, then read **कुआँ** and say what it means]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "HEAR",
