              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *desh*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "READ",
              "instruction": "देश (desh), then say what it means",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU READ: देश, then say what it means]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does देश (desh) mean? (\"a country\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HI-C68-india",
      "sequence": 2620,
      "title": "भारत (Bhārat) — India",
      "headword": "भारत",
      "romanization": "Bhārat",
      "gloss": "India",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:fa4da7418440ec68",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say desh, then write देश from memory. Three letters and one matra: द, then े on top of it, then श. You have been taught all three."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: भारत",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भारत (Bhārat) — \"India\", the country's name in its own language."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The name is older than the country. भरत (Bharata) is a figure the Sanskrit epics name, and भारत (Bhārat) is the form meaning \"belonging to Bharata\" — the land of his people. English India took a different route entirely, through Greek and Persian from सिंधु (Sindhu), the river."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "So one country carries two names that started as two different things: a people and a river. In Hindi you will hear भारत (Bhārat) on the news and हिंदुस्तान in the street, and both mean the same place."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A देश (desh) and the name of one: भारत (Bhārat) एक देश (desh) है."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "RECALL",
              "instruction": "read कुआँ, then say it without looking",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU RECALL: read **कुआँ**, then say it without looking]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "Bhārat",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *Bhārat*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "Bhārat ek desh hai",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *Bhārat ek desh hai*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "a नाम line with no model, then देश (desh) on the line under it",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: a नाम line with no model, then देश on the line under it]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "देश (desh) once more, without looking",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: देश once more, without looking]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does भारत (Bhārat) mean? (\"India\".) And देश (desh)? (\"a country\".)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
