    {
      "id": "HI-C68-city",
      "sequence": 2630,
      "title": "शहर (shahar) — a city, a town",
      "headword": "शहर",
      "romanization": "shahar",
      "gloss": "a city, a town",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:ceea1ec2ea2229c0",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which of the two words you have is the name of a country, and which is the word for any country at all?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: शहर",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शहर (shahar) — \"a city, a town\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Persian شهر (shahr), \"city\", and behind it Old Persian xšaça, \"kingdom, dominion\" — a शहर (shahar) was first the seat of a king rather than a crowd of people. The same word ends dozens of place names across the region."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Set it against गाँव (gā̃v), the village you already own. गाँव and शहर (shahar) are the pair Hindi uses for the whole of settled life, and a speaker will place themselves in one or the other within a sentence of meeting you."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A form asks for your शहर (shahar) on the line under your देश (desh)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three: देश (desh), भारत (Bhārat), शहर (shahar). A country, its name, and the place in it you live."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "HEAR",
              "instruction": "shahar, then gā̃v",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU HEAR: *shahar*, then *gā̃v*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "shahar",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *shahar*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "CONTRAST",
              "instruction": "shahar and gā̃v, and say which one is bigger",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU CONTRAST: *shahar* and *gā̃v*, and say which one is bigger]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does शहर (shahar) mean? (\"a city\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "HI-C68-language",
      "sequence": 2640,
      "title": "भाषा (bhāshā) — a language",
      "headword": "भाषा",
      "romanization": "bhāshā",
      "gloss": "a language",
      "script": "devanagari",
      "modality": "voice",
      "derivedModality": "voice",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "no-visual-dependency"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:63ed2135d6307f84",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Write शहर (shahar) from memory: श, then ह, then र. No matras at all in this one — three bare letters in a row."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: भाषा",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "भाषा (bhāshā) — \"a language\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit भाषा (bhāshā) (bhāṣā), \"speech, what is spoken\", from भाष् (bhāṣ-), \"to speak\". The word names the act before it names the thing: a भाषा (bhāshā) is speaking, turned into a noun."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You have been saying मैं हिंदी बोलता हूँ for a long time. भाषा (bhāshā) is the word that lets you talk about हिंदी rather than only in it — and it is a printed line on both of the writing papers you will one day sit, right under देश (desh) and शहर (shahar)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four of the five lines a form asks for: देश (desh), भारत (Bhārat), शहर (shahar), भाषा (bhāshā)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
